//? Title: Character CNN:raw review bytes and visible momentum SGD
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Original movie-review bytes feed fixed onehot ingress and the full six-convolution topology. Explicit tensor count fits and all60 momentum SGD updates expose poor held-out results and the different word/byte observation views.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.9_1d_convolutions/character_cnn.cpp`.

> The method

Reverse the last256 raw source bytes,mask unknown/padded positions,and apply six valid convolutions with three pools and two dense dropout layers. Show tensor Momentum SGD directly,select on validation CE,and restore18 leaves for independent character-only inference.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/character_cnn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/character_cnn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/character_cnn_concept.tikz > build/character_cnn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/character_cnn_concept.svg build/character_cnn_concept.dvi > build/character_cnn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
