> Full and compact topology, without synthetic text claims

The full source-small binary graph usesT1014,C256,dense1024;the actual fit
usesT256,C16,dense64. Both preserve18 learned tensors and every convolution,
pool and dense layer. The binary head and source initialization are teaching
adaptations of Zhang/Zhao/LeCun,not an exact paper training reproduction.
The declared all-known shape probe below is a structural fixture,not real text.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/character_cnn_shapes.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::print("| graph | input length | channels | dense | learned values | leaves | flattened "
             "|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n");
  for (bool compact : {false, true}) {
    const auto c = compact ? m::CharacterConfig{256, 16, 64, 69} : m::CharacterConfig{};
    n::ParameterStore p(2);
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    const auto out = m::CharacterCnn(p, n::zeros({1, c.time}, n::DType::Int32),
                                     n::full({1}, c.time, n::DType::Int32), c);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", compact ? "actual compact" : "full",
               c.time, c.channels, c.dense, p.count(), p.size(), out.flat.shape());
  }
  std::vector<double> lengths;
  for (int length : {250, 83, 77, 25, 23, 21, 19, 17, 5})
    lengths.push_back(length);
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(n::arange(1, 10).to_vector<double>(), lengths, "compact stages", {37, 99, 235})
      .title("Six valid convolutions and three pools")
      .x_label("stage:conv1,pool1,conv2,pool2,conv3..6,pool6")
      .y_label("retained temporal length");
  plot.save_svg("build/character_cnn_shapes.svg");
}
