> Verification and limits

Six native tests cover the raw-byte encoder,all62 tiny host finite-difference
coordinates,the full11335938-scalar graph and every learned derivative,every
original1400-row byte encoding/length/label/ID and word alignment,all counts,
retained host NB scores,explicit SGD parity,unknown holes and padding controls.
Every public example compiles and runs. The original full checks and genuine
three-epoch workflow pass. This short fit stays near chance;the selected model
is worse than the declared count references. Lower fitting loss does not
establish useful held-out accuracy or published large-corpus performance.

> Conclusion

The short character CNN fit has limited held-out sentiment accuracy. Every optimization step,original row alignment,source-byte policy and unchanged count reference remains visible so the report supports implementation checks without a benchmark claim.

> References

- [Zhang,Zhao and LeCun(2015),Character-level Convolutional Networks for Text Classification](https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.01626).
- [Official Pang/Lee MR sentence-polarity data](https://www.cs.cornell.edu/people/pabo/movie-review-data/).
